00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:10,657
[dishes rattling]

2
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,744
[Heeju] I wanted to run away
from the pawn shop.

3
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:18,290
But there was a shadow of misfortune
that fell on my shoulders.

4
00:00:18,373 --> 00:00:21,793
It was a weight
that I just couldn't shake off.

5
00:00:24,004 --> 00:00:25,088
[gasps]

6
00:00:25,172 --> 00:00:28,175
[flies buzzing]

7
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:30,886
[creaking]

8
00:00:30,969 --> 00:00:33,138
[inhales and exhales sharply]

9
00:00:35,974 --> 00:00:38,560
[Cheoljung] Do you know
how worried I've been?

10
00:00:38,644 --> 00:00:40,228
You've got a perfectly good home.

11
00:00:40,312 --> 00:00:41,688
Why are you putting yourself through this?

12
00:00:41,772 --> 00:00:44,566
Oh, no! Mm!

13
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,318
[Cheoljung] Look at you.
Your poor hands.

14
00:00:46,401 --> 00:00:49,237
Whatever. Can you just go now?

15
00:00:50,155 --> 00:00:51,948
[exhales]

16
00:00:52,032 --> 00:00:53,492
'Kay, I'll go.

17
00:00:53,575 --> 00:00:55,535
[Cheoljung] But you should
come home more often.

18
00:00:56,495 --> 00:00:58,955
We can all have dinner together, yeah?

19
00:01:02,626 --> 00:01:04,461
[inhales on cigarette]

20
00:01:07,506 --> 00:01:09,549
Gross. That bastard.

21
00:01:14,429 --> 00:01:18,809
[Heeju] I swore to myself I would never
be lured by that light that got my mother.

22
00:01:19,976 --> 00:01:22,020
I needed a light of my own.

23
00:01:22,104 --> 00:01:23,897
One that would hide me from my shadow.

24
00:01:25,232 --> 00:01:28,694
But without money,
you don't have a lot of options.

25
00:01:31,947 --> 00:01:32,864
[roulette wheel rattling]

26
00:01:32,948 --> 00:01:35,951
[Heeju] Gold Land makes promises
of dazzling fortune.

27
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:37,869
But that's not what I dreamed of.

28
00:01:39,121 --> 00:01:44,584
Maybe all I wanted was just some guarantee
that I could be safe here.

29
00:01:45,502 --> 00:01:47,462
It was all someone like me could hope for.

30
00:01:47,546 --> 00:01:49,256
[indistinct chatter]

31
00:01:54,302 --> 00:01:57,097
[chips clinking]

32
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,348
[Male Gambler] Hey, hey, hey, hey.

33
00:01:58,432 --> 00:02:01,184
-What's the deal with these red ones?
-[Heeju] Sorry?

34
00:02:01,268 --> 00:02:03,728
They're all supposed to be yellow.
I exchanged them for yellow!

35
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,481
Ch-change it!

36
00:02:07,899 --> 00:02:09,734
Hey! Hear me or what?

37
00:02:09,818 --> 00:02:11,528
-[Guard A] All right, that's enough.
-Do you think I'm stupid, bitch?

38
00:02:11,611 --> 00:02:13,822
-[Guard A] Time to go, sir.
-[Guard B] Let's go.

39
00:02:13,905 --> 00:02:15,824
[Male Gambler] Let go of me!
Get your hands off me!

40
00:02:15,907 --> 00:02:19,077
-Call the manager! Call the manager now!
-[Guard A] Get him out. Let's go!

41
00:02:19,161 --> 00:02:20,412
[Dokyung] What the hell?

42
00:02:21,079 --> 00:02:22,247
What's up with that guy?

43
00:02:26,543 --> 00:02:28,545
Oh.

44
00:02:28,628 --> 00:02:30,881
100 gold chips, please.

45
00:02:32,174 --> 00:02:34,676
[Heeju] That's when he walked
into my life.

46
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:38,472
A man who seemed to be made
of nothing but good luck.

47
00:02:38,555 --> 00:02:42,058
He was like a mirage
that came out of nowhere.

48
00:02:42,142 --> 00:02:43,810
Something that didn't belong in my world.

49
00:02:44,728 --> 00:02:46,897
As if he'd disappear if I touched him.

50
00:02:48,231 --> 00:02:51,777
Time to see if luck is on
my side today.

51
00:02:54,070 --> 00:02:55,405
[Dokyung] Thank you, Miss Heeju.
STYLE
::cue()

52
00:03:05,123 --> 00:03:07,459
[Dokyung] I bought this on my way back
from Hong Kong. It's for you.

53
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,003
Heard you like planes, so...

54
00:03:13,215 --> 00:03:16,843
Uh, 100 gold chips, please.

55
00:03:21,723 --> 00:03:23,016
[machine rattling]

56
00:03:31,608 --> 00:03:33,026
[Dokyung exhales sharply]

57
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:37,906
Time to see if luck is on my side today.

58
00:03:41,451 --> 00:03:42,661
Thank you.

59
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,505
[Dokyung exhaling]

60
00:03:53,588 --> 00:03:55,006
[Dokyung] Whew!

61
00:03:55,090 --> 00:03:57,676
[all gasping and laughing]

62
00:04:00,929 --> 00:04:01,972
[woman gasps]

63
00:04:02,055 --> 00:04:02,973
Yes!

64
00:04:03,056 --> 00:04:04,558
[crowd cheering]

65
00:04:04,641 --> 00:04:06,309
[applause]

66
00:04:09,437 --> 00:04:10,772
[Woman] Did you see that?

67
00:04:10,855 --> 00:04:14,526
[Dokyung breathing heavily]

68
00:04:15,902 --> 00:04:19,406
Hey, see this?
It's yours Heeju.

69
00:04:20,532 --> 00:04:22,158
I only won it because of you.

70
00:04:22,242 --> 00:04:23,493
[scoffs]

71
00:04:30,166 --> 00:04:31,626
[exhales]

72
00:04:33,044 --> 00:04:34,045
Uh...

73
00:04:35,005 --> 00:04:38,717
[indistinct chatter]

74
00:04:47,809 --> 00:04:49,269
[Cheoljung inhales deeply]

75
00:04:49,352 --> 00:04:52,439
Give me some gold chips,
why don't ya?

76
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:57,569
This is where you were hiding, huh?

77
00:04:58,612 --> 00:05:01,072
[Cheoljung] Do you have any idea
how long I've been looking for you?

78
00:05:03,658 --> 00:05:05,201
[Heeju] Get out.

79
00:05:05,285 --> 00:05:07,245
I don't have anything to say to you.

80
00:05:07,329 --> 00:05:08,955
That's no way to talk to your uncle.

81
00:05:09,039 --> 00:05:12,792
Like it or not,
the two of us are family, ya know.

82
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:14,377
You are not my family.

83
00:05:15,503 --> 00:05:17,505
Hmm.

84
00:05:18,256 --> 00:05:20,300
But you're my sweet little niece.

85
00:05:21,217 --> 00:05:22,802
[hiccups and grunts]

86
00:05:22,886 --> 00:05:25,931
Enough of this.
Let's just go home now.

87
00:05:26,014 --> 00:05:28,642
Did my aunt tell you, then?
Where to find me?

88
00:05:28,725 --> 00:05:29,643
[Cheoljung] Of course.

89
00:05:29,726 --> 00:05:31,227
She was worried sick.

90
00:05:31,311 --> 00:05:33,355
[Cheoljung] You're her only niece.

91
00:05:33,438 --> 00:05:36,191
Come back home now, really.
Heeju.

92
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:38,109
-[Cheoljung] Do you really think...
-Security, he's drunk.

93
00:05:38,193 --> 00:05:41,488
...you can live in Jeongsan
without me finding out about it?

94
00:05:41,571 --> 00:05:42,614
-[Guard A] Let's go, let's go.
-[Cheoljung] Come on.

95
00:05:42,697 --> 00:05:45,241
[Cheoljung] I'm this girl's uncle, okay?

96
00:05:45,325 --> 00:05:48,578
Ah, shitheads!
Get the hell off of me!

97
00:05:48,662 --> 00:05:50,288
[Cheoljung] She's my niece!
I'm telling you!

98
00:05:50,372 --> 00:05:52,123
-[Guard B] Come on!
-Be sure to eat well, okay?

99
00:05:53,041 --> 00:05:55,460
-[Cheoljung] You've lost weight, you know!
-[Heeju] Even the light of this place

100
00:05:55,543 --> 00:05:57,712
-couldn't conceal my shadow.
-[Cheoljung] I'll be back for you! Heeju!
STYLE
::cue()

101
00:05:57,796 --> 00:06:04,260
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

102
00:06:04,886 --> 00:06:06,972
[Heeju] How much longer could I endure?

103
00:06:08,181 --> 00:06:09,766
Like my mother...

104
00:06:10,767 --> 00:06:12,519
...I was already starting to wither.

105
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:17,065
I felt like I couldn't go on much longer.

106
00:06:18,108 --> 00:06:19,567
I had to reach for it.

107
00:06:20,902 --> 00:06:23,905
Even if it was just
a mirage that would disappear.

108
00:06:23,989 --> 00:06:26,992
[♪ sad music]

109
00:06:33,164 --> 00:06:34,165
[door lock beeps]

110
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:36,334
[door opens]

111
00:06:56,479 --> 00:06:57,480
Heeju.

112
00:07:06,656 --> 00:07:07,657
Here you go.

113
00:07:08,658 --> 00:07:11,077
I exchanged those chips you gave me
into cash for you.

114
00:07:11,619 --> 00:07:12,620
[inhales sharply]

115
00:07:14,205 --> 00:07:18,084
Uh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean it that way.

116
00:07:19,252 --> 00:07:20,503
What did you mean, then?

117
00:07:20,587 --> 00:07:25,550
Well, either way it was up to you
to decide whether to come here or not.

118
00:07:28,386 --> 00:07:30,430
[Dokyung] But take this at least.

119
00:07:30,513 --> 00:07:32,766
As a token of my appreciation.

120
00:07:33,725 --> 00:07:35,310
[grunts]

121
00:07:38,104 --> 00:07:39,898
[Heeju] This is everything I have.

122
00:07:39,981 --> 00:07:43,318
Take the money and place
a single bet for me.

123
00:07:44,444 --> 00:07:46,196
[Heeju] I've decided to trust you.

124
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:47,781
And for once in my life...

125
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:51,618
...take a gamble and see if my life
has any luck at all.

126
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:58,708
[Female Dealer] The game at table two
will start in one minute.

127
00:07:58,792 --> 00:08:00,543
[Female Dealer] You have one minute
if you want to play.

128
00:08:01,628 --> 00:08:04,589
[crowd cheering]

129
00:08:04,672 --> 00:08:06,007
[Dokyung] Congrats, Heeju.
Good job.

130
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:08,676
You won.
The pot is all yours.

131
00:08:10,428 --> 00:08:11,971
[chips rattling]

132
00:08:12,055 --> 00:08:13,431
[Heeju exhales]

133
00:08:13,515 --> 00:08:15,099
Wait a sec, Heeju.

134
00:08:15,183 --> 00:08:16,392
Just a sec.

135
00:08:18,228 --> 00:08:20,396
-[Heeju gasping]
-It's okay.

136
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:23,233
-[Dokyung] It's okay.
-[Heeju] Wait. I don't...

137
00:08:23,316 --> 00:08:25,235
Let's place these ones on top.

138
00:08:25,318 --> 00:08:26,653
What?

139
00:08:28,822 --> 00:08:30,448
Trust me, Heeju.

140
00:08:33,493 --> 00:08:36,496
[♪ hopeful music]

141
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,001
[Heeju exhales]

142
00:08:46,631 --> 00:08:48,299
[Dokyung exhales]

143
00:08:52,011 --> 00:08:53,638
[Heeju sighs]

144
00:08:56,349 --> 00:08:59,769
[crowd whispering]

145
00:09:02,147 --> 00:09:03,189
[both exhale]

146
00:09:03,273 --> 00:09:04,440
Ten.

147
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:08,111
[Heeju exhales]

148
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,321
[Dokyung] Okay.

149
00:09:11,197 --> 00:09:14,576
[cheers and applause]

150
00:09:14,659 --> 00:09:16,536
[Heeju gasps]

151
00:09:16,619 --> 00:09:18,830
Heeju! Heeju, you did it!

152
00:09:18,913 --> 00:09:20,748
You won it all!

153
00:09:22,458 --> 00:09:24,502
[Dokyung] Okay, these are yours.

154
00:09:24,586 --> 00:09:26,004
[Heeju gasps]

155
00:09:26,087 --> 00:09:27,630
This is enough, right?

156
00:09:27,714 --> 00:09:29,048
Congratulations.

157
00:09:30,550 --> 00:09:34,345
[Heeju] From then on,
for the first time in my life,

158
00:09:34,429 --> 00:09:37,098
it finally felt like there
was a light in my world.

159
00:09:38,474 --> 00:09:40,518
Like I was seeing the sun
for the first time

160
00:09:40,602 --> 00:09:42,562
after coming out of a dark tunnel.

161
00:09:43,438 --> 00:09:48,067
It was warm and everything around me
was crystal clear.

162
00:09:48,151 --> 00:09:49,110
-Come here.
-What?

163
00:09:49,194 --> 00:09:52,822
[Heeju] Every moment,
every day filled with gratitude.

164
00:09:52,906 --> 00:09:54,365
I was happy.

165
00:09:55,783 --> 00:09:58,244
What, you don't like mine?
What's not to like?

166
00:09:58,328 --> 00:10:01,789
[indistinct chatter]
STYLE
::cue()

167
00:10:08,713 --> 00:10:09,714
[Dokyung] What are you staring at?

168
00:10:13,509 --> 00:10:16,387
[Heeju] Am I really allowed
to live like this?

169
00:10:16,471 --> 00:10:17,597
[Dokyung] What does that mean?

170
00:10:19,599 --> 00:10:20,975
Just like this.

171
00:10:22,936 --> 00:10:24,270
Like other people.

172
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,856
Happy and calm.

173
00:10:29,776 --> 00:10:31,945
You met me,
so you must be lucky.

174
00:10:33,154 --> 00:10:34,781
[chuckles]

175
00:10:34,864 --> 00:10:37,450
You're the first person
to ever say that to me.

176
00:10:38,701 --> 00:10:40,203
Ever since I was a kid,

177
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:43,122
everyone always told me I
was an unlucky little brat.

178
00:10:44,499 --> 00:10:45,750
[Heeju] And it was kind of true.

179
00:10:46,834 --> 00:10:48,753
So none of this feels real.

180
00:10:49,712 --> 00:10:51,464
Being happy like this.

181
00:10:53,675 --> 00:10:54,717
Being with you.

182
00:10:54,801 --> 00:10:56,678
[inhales and exhales sharply]

183
00:10:58,721 --> 00:11:00,223
Isn't happiness meant for everyone?

184
00:11:00,306 --> 00:11:01,307
Mm.

185
00:11:02,350 --> 00:11:04,519
[Dokyung] You don't have
to worry about anything now.

186
00:11:05,436 --> 00:11:06,980
Just trust me and follow my lead.

187
00:11:07,814 --> 00:11:09,357
This is barely the beginning.

188
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,359
[Dokyung] From this moment on...

189
00:11:12,485 --> 00:11:16,239
...I'm gonna show you exactly
how lucky you are.

190
00:11:18,908 --> 00:11:19,909
Santé?

191
00:11:22,245 --> 00:11:23,371
[exhales]

192
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:24,998
Santé.

193
00:11:25,081 --> 00:11:26,666
[glasses clink]

194
00:11:34,632 --> 00:11:37,343
[distant seagulls cawing]

195
00:11:40,138 --> 00:11:42,348
[Heeju giggles]

196
00:11:45,018 --> 00:11:51,024
NO ENTRY

197
00:11:57,447 --> 00:12:00,450
[♪ suspenseful music]

198
00:12:29,771 --> 00:12:30,772
[grunts]

199
00:12:45,286 --> 00:12:46,579
[Heeju] Is this mine?

200
00:12:48,122 --> 00:12:49,123
No.

201
00:12:50,333 --> 00:12:52,210
Then is it Lee Dokyung's?

202
00:12:53,586 --> 00:12:54,962
Also no.

203
00:12:56,714 --> 00:12:58,174
I don't know whose it is.

204
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,511
Maybe I don't wanna know.

205
00:13:02,428 --> 00:13:04,722
But if it doesn't belong
to anyone anyway,

206
00:13:04,806 --> 00:13:05,807
why shouldn't I take it?

207
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:09,727
At least,
that's what I kept telling myself.

208
00:13:11,270 --> 00:13:13,314
You're just doing what Lee Dokyung
told you to do.

209
00:13:14,232 --> 00:13:16,067
You can't help it because you love him.

210
00:13:16,776 --> 00:13:18,111
That's what you think, right?

211
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,864
Did I really love Lee Dokyung?

212
00:13:21,948 --> 00:13:24,909
Or was it that I just wanted to escape?

213
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:27,995
Did it really matter?

214
00:13:30,456 --> 00:13:36,129
No, but now I have
to decide for myself.

215
00:13:36,879 --> 00:13:40,049
What does it really mean to be happy?

216
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,845
[inhales and exhales sharply]

217
00:13:43,928 --> 00:13:46,931
[♪ sad piano music]

218
00:14:05,658 --> 00:14:08,661
[♪ music continues]
STYLE
::cue()

219
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:29,015
EPISODE 4
HIM

220
00:14:29,098 --> 00:14:31,517
[Jinman] Stop bugging me about it, okay?

221
00:14:32,059 --> 00:14:33,227
I'll find it soon.

222
00:14:33,311 --> 00:14:34,562
[indistinct chatter]

223
00:14:34,645 --> 00:14:36,564
Yes, I know that.

224
00:14:36,647 --> 00:14:38,691
The chairman will be back next week?

225
00:14:38,774 --> 00:14:40,651
[Jinman] I'll get back
to you as soon as I can.

226
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,445
Yeah.

227
00:14:42,528 --> 00:14:43,779
[exhales]

228
00:14:43,863 --> 00:14:45,865
[Jinman] Oh! Ah!

229
00:14:45,948 --> 00:14:47,867
Ah, fuck me.

230
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:49,243
Seriously?

231
00:14:49,327 --> 00:14:52,330
[indistinct chatter]

232
00:15:00,254 --> 00:15:02,506
Ah, shit.

233
00:15:05,218 --> 00:15:06,928
[mouse wheel scrolling]

234
00:15:07,011 --> 00:15:08,471
Is that a woman?

235
00:15:27,573 --> 00:15:30,493
WITNESS STATEMENT RECORD
WITNESS PERSONAL INFORMATION

236
00:15:37,416 --> 00:15:38,834
[Male Detective] And your name?

237
00:15:40,670 --> 00:15:42,046
[Sunok] Yeo Sunok.

238
00:15:45,216 --> 00:15:46,217
[Male Detective exhales sharply]

239
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:47,885
[Male Detective] Around what time
did this happen?

240
00:15:50,805 --> 00:15:51,889
Um...

241
00:15:52,807 --> 00:15:55,518
[Sunok] Last night.
Around 10:00.

242
00:15:55,601 --> 00:15:57,520
[Male Detective] Okay, around 10:00 p.m.

243
00:15:57,603 --> 00:15:58,729
Afternoon, sir.

244
00:15:58,813 --> 00:16:00,064
-Wait!
-Yeah?

245
00:16:00,648 --> 00:16:02,108
Well, that woman.

246
00:16:02,191 --> 00:16:03,943
[Jinman] What's her deal?

247
00:16:04,026 --> 00:16:04,986
Ah, her?

248
00:16:05,069 --> 00:16:06,570
She was booked this morning
at a local precinct,

249
00:16:06,654 --> 00:16:07,655
but they handed it over to us.

250
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:10,533
She bashed her husband with a golf club.
He's in the hospital.

251
00:16:10,616 --> 00:16:11,909
Her husband reported it?

252
00:16:11,993 --> 00:16:14,370
No, she reported it herself.

253
00:16:14,453 --> 00:16:15,705
[Jinman] What about the husband?

254
00:16:15,788 --> 00:16:17,081
He wants to press charges.

255
00:16:17,164 --> 00:16:20,334
According to him, she-
she was after his pawnshop's money.

256
00:16:20,418 --> 00:16:23,212
-Says he has evidence.
-[Mija] Sunok!

257
00:16:23,296 --> 00:16:26,549
Sunok! What's going on here?
Is it true?

258
00:16:26,632 --> 00:16:28,592
-Well, I'll be going.
-[grunts]

259
00:16:28,676 --> 00:16:30,636
-You didn't really do it, did you?
-Hi, there.

260
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,096
[Male Detective]
Are you a family member?

261
00:16:32,179 --> 00:16:34,432
No, but she's like a sister.

262
00:16:34,515 --> 00:16:35,725
How did you find out?

263
00:16:35,808 --> 00:16:36,892
What are you saying?

264
00:16:36,976 --> 00:16:39,145
You called me to come and get you.

265
00:16:41,439 --> 00:16:43,274
Can you make sure she leaves?

266
00:16:43,357 --> 00:16:45,318
Sunok, dammit,
that's not what should concern you.

267
00:16:45,401 --> 00:16:46,986
[Mija] You shouldn't be here.

268
00:16:48,154 --> 00:16:50,281
[Mija] Detective, this woman
is very sick.

269
00:16:50,364 --> 00:16:52,408
She has terminal cancer.

270
00:16:54,577 --> 00:16:57,163
[Mija] I mean, she should be in
the hospital, not in a place like this!

271
00:16:57,246 --> 00:16:59,582
[Male Detective] I understand, but I
still have to continue processing her.

272
00:17:00,499 --> 00:17:02,501
-Detective, please!
-Jeongsan-gun.

273
00:17:02,585 --> 00:17:05,463
-Sunok!
-Five, dash, 18 Bukju.

274
00:17:05,546 --> 00:17:06,881
Detective!

275
00:17:06,964 --> 00:17:09,967
SAMJEON JEWELRY DEPARTMENT STORE

276
00:17:10,926 --> 00:17:13,429
[Woogy] Ah, okay.
No, no, no, no.

277
00:17:14,221 --> 00:17:15,389
Excuse me.

278
00:17:17,850 --> 00:17:19,352
Yeah, sure thing.

279
00:17:19,435 --> 00:17:20,770
Thank you. Mm.

280
00:17:21,395 --> 00:17:22,646
[inhales sharply]

281
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:26,400
We could have made preparations
if you had called ahead of time.

282
00:17:26,484 --> 00:17:27,526
[Male Store Owner] Sorry about that.

283
00:17:30,112 --> 00:17:32,365
But we'll buy the gold bar.
We'll have the cash ready soon.

284
00:17:32,448 --> 00:17:33,491
[Male Store Owner] Do you mind waiting
a little longer?

285
00:17:33,574 --> 00:17:34,450
Of course.

286
00:17:34,533 --> 00:17:35,993
[chuckles]

287
00:17:38,287 --> 00:17:39,955
[exhales]

288
00:17:43,626 --> 00:17:45,961
Uh, sir. Excuse me.

289
00:17:47,088 --> 00:17:49,507
This one here.
Can I buy this?

290
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:51,634
Uh, would you like to look
at that one, too?

291
00:17:51,717 --> 00:17:53,719
-Heh, yeah.
-Sure. Just one minute.

292
00:18:00,976 --> 00:18:02,186
[Female Store Owner] You want it in cash?

293
00:18:02,269 --> 00:18:03,979
130 million?

294
00:18:04,063 --> 00:18:05,272
Yeah.

295
00:18:05,356 --> 00:18:06,816
[exhale sharply]

296
00:18:06,899 --> 00:18:08,275
If you can't do it, don't worry.

297
00:18:08,359 --> 00:18:09,694
-I'll go somewhere else.
-Oh, no, no, no, no.

298
00:18:09,777 --> 00:18:12,238
[chuckles nervously]
Wait just a minute.

299
00:18:13,155 --> 00:18:14,365
[exhales]

300
00:18:16,409 --> 00:18:18,577
[Female Customer] Honey, I want this one!

301
00:18:18,661 --> 00:18:20,538
-Isn't it beautiful?
-Really?

302
00:18:20,621 --> 00:18:22,248
You don't want this one?
It's shiny.

303
00:18:22,331 --> 00:18:23,833
Happy with that little thing?

304
00:18:23,916 --> 00:18:25,251
[chuckles]

305
00:18:26,085 --> 00:18:27,086
[grunts]

306
00:18:30,005 --> 00:18:32,007
[breathing heavily]

307
00:18:35,219 --> 00:18:36,470
You don't want to count to make sure?

308
00:18:36,554 --> 00:18:39,849
I plan on doing more business with you,
so I'm sure it's the right amount.

309
00:18:39,932 --> 00:18:41,392
Ah, yes.

310
00:18:41,475 --> 00:18:42,518
[inhales sharply]

311
00:18:42,601 --> 00:18:44,937
TRANSFEREE: KIM MINCHEOL

312
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,689
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KIM MINCHEOL
STYLE
::cue()

313
00:18:46,772 --> 00:18:48,441
JEWELRY WORLD

314
00:18:48,524 --> 00:18:50,276
[cell phone vibrating]

315
00:18:50,359 --> 00:18:52,153
Heeju, what's up?

316
00:18:52,236 --> 00:18:53,237
[Heeju] Where are you?

317
00:18:54,155 --> 00:18:55,698
Where do you think? Daejeong.

318
00:18:56,615 --> 00:18:58,367
Just finishing up with the potatoes.

319
00:18:58,826 --> 00:18:59,827
Where are you?

320
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:01,162
You don't need to know.

321
00:19:02,455 --> 00:19:04,665
I need you to just show me where you
are right now.

322
00:19:04,749 --> 00:19:07,084
[Woogy] Ah, why can't you just trust me?

323
00:19:09,336 --> 00:19:11,338
See? Jewelry stores.

324
00:19:12,715 --> 00:19:13,716
[Woogy] By the way,

325
00:19:13,799 --> 00:19:15,176
I think I'm gonna get a new car.

326
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:17,887
[Woogy] I'm young and rich now.

327
00:19:18,804 --> 00:19:20,598
This car doesn't cut it anymore.
[car alarm beeps]

328
00:19:22,349 --> 00:19:23,392
[exhales sharply]

329
00:19:23,476 --> 00:19:26,687
[Woogy] Well anyway,
I'll be headed over there later.

330
00:19:26,771 --> 00:19:29,690
You just, uh, bring the gold.

331
00:19:30,316 --> 00:19:31,358
See you soon.

332
00:19:35,321 --> 00:19:36,322
[exhales sharply]

333
00:19:37,907 --> 00:19:40,785
[lightly chuckling]

334
00:19:44,914 --> 00:19:45,998
[car alarm beeps]

335
00:19:49,251 --> 00:19:52,254
[♪ suspenseful music]

336
00:19:56,342 --> 00:20:00,179
YANGPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

337
00:20:04,642 --> 00:20:06,310
[coughing]

338
00:20:10,231 --> 00:20:11,232
[car alarm beeps]

339
00:20:34,797 --> 00:20:35,798
[camera shutter clicks]

340
00:20:37,258 --> 00:20:38,259
[door opens]

341
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:40,886
[camera shutter clicks]

342
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:41,971
And who are you?

343
00:20:42,054 --> 00:20:45,766
Oh, uh, hi.
Jeongsan Police Department.

344
00:20:45,850 --> 00:20:48,727
Uh, Detective Kim Jinman.

345
00:20:48,811 --> 00:20:51,230
Here's my business card for you.

346
00:20:51,313 --> 00:20:53,023
[Yujin] The Jeongsan Police?

347
00:20:53,107 --> 00:20:55,818
I thought that my team was cleared
of any involvement

348
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:57,444
and the investigation was over.

349
00:20:57,528 --> 00:20:59,405
Yeah, sort of.

350
00:20:59,488 --> 00:21:01,949
This particular case has become so complex

351
00:21:02,032 --> 00:21:04,243
that we're conducting
a joint investigation.

352
00:21:04,326 --> 00:21:06,537
And regarding Mr. Lee Dokyung,

353
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:08,038
we haven't caught the suspect
for the hit-and-run.

354
00:21:09,915 --> 00:21:12,459
So the police still haven't been able
to find the casket?

355
00:21:12,543 --> 00:21:15,296
-No, not yet.
-[Yujin] Hmm.

356
00:21:15,379 --> 00:21:16,964
What do you want to ask me about, exactly?

357
00:21:18,090 --> 00:21:19,383
You're close with Lee Dokyung, right?

358
00:21:19,466 --> 00:21:20,718
You two call each other a lot?

359
00:21:21,802 --> 00:21:23,137
Because of work, I guess.

360
00:21:23,721 --> 00:21:25,890
There's nothing going on between us.

361
00:21:25,973 --> 00:21:27,558
[exhales sharply]

362
00:21:27,641 --> 00:21:29,393
It's been a while since we've talked.

363
00:21:30,561 --> 00:21:31,854
So what's going on?

364
00:21:32,521 --> 00:21:34,023
[inhales sharply]

365
00:21:34,106 --> 00:21:36,233
I don't really know,
but I might need a favor.

366
00:21:36,317 --> 00:21:37,985
[Yujin inhales on cigarette]

367
00:21:38,068 --> 00:21:40,237
Could you get something through customs
for me?

368
00:21:40,321 --> 00:21:42,364
[exhales]
Favor?

369
00:21:43,741 --> 00:21:44,992
Why?

370
00:21:45,075 --> 00:21:47,119
Why not just tell me you love me
like you used to?

371
00:21:48,329 --> 00:21:49,872
[Yujin] You can't say it anymore?

372
00:21:51,749 --> 00:21:54,043
You said it just fine
when you were cheating on me.

373
00:21:54,710 --> 00:21:57,713
This is important.
I'm not playing around here.

374
00:21:57,796 --> 00:22:00,633
[Jinman] You spoke with him on the phone
on the day of the accident, the fourth.

375
00:22:01,634 --> 00:22:02,718
[exhales sharply]

376
00:22:02,801 --> 00:22:05,596
Was I the only person who spoke
to Lee Dokyung that day?

377
00:22:05,679 --> 00:22:06,680
[Jinman] Not at all.

378
00:22:06,764 --> 00:22:08,766
Miss, this is just standard procedure.

379
00:22:08,849 --> 00:22:10,059
I have to ask, 'kay?

380
00:22:11,226 --> 00:22:12,728
Lee Dokyung, what did he say?

381
00:22:12,811 --> 00:22:13,938
FIRST OFFICER LEE DOKYUNG:

382
00:22:14,021 --> 00:22:15,814
THIS IS THE LAST TIME.
PLEASE JUST COME ONE MORE TIME TOMORROW.

383
00:22:15,898 --> 00:22:17,900
I CAN GIVE YOU WHAT YOU REALLY WANT.
NATIONAL ROUTE 6, 50-7

384
00:22:20,694 --> 00:22:22,571
[Yujin] We just talked
about personal stuff.

385
00:22:23,822 --> 00:22:26,033
But I don't really feel like getting
into all that right now.

386
00:22:26,116 --> 00:22:27,493
Oh.

387
00:22:28,661 --> 00:22:32,122
So you're close enough to speak
about personal matters on the phone. Mm.

388
00:22:32,206 --> 00:22:34,500
[Jinman] The day of the accident, then.

389
00:22:35,084 --> 00:22:37,461
Do you happen to know anyone who
could verify where you were?

390
00:22:38,379 --> 00:22:39,505
My alibi?

391
00:22:39,588 --> 00:22:41,173
Your alibi, yeah.

392
00:22:41,256 --> 00:22:42,675
You've already gone through
my call history.
STYLE
::cue()

393
00:22:42,758 --> 00:22:44,259
Shouldn't you already know?

394
00:22:44,343 --> 00:22:45,970
You see, the thing is,

395
00:22:46,053 --> 00:22:49,348
we can't verify anything you did after
the call with Lee Dokyung.

396
00:22:49,431 --> 00:22:52,518
At 10:00 p.m., you turned your phone off
for the rest of the night.

397
00:22:52,601 --> 00:22:55,437
[Yujin] Well, I would have been home
at that time.

398
00:22:55,521 --> 00:22:56,605
Mm-hmm.

399
00:22:57,731 --> 00:23:00,609
Ah, wait.
I went to the theater that night.

400
00:23:00,693 --> 00:23:02,486
For a late night movie.

401
00:23:02,569 --> 00:23:04,863
Movie theater?
Which theater did you go to?

402
00:23:04,947 --> 00:23:06,156
The theater in Sokcho.

403
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:08,701
Alone or with someone?

404
00:23:09,618 --> 00:23:11,996
-I went alone.
-[Jinman] I see.

405
00:23:12,079 --> 00:23:14,456
[groaning]

406
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:18,168
Do you happen to have anything that you
can show me like a ticket stub

407
00:23:18,252 --> 00:23:20,587
or reservation E-mail that shows you
were there that night?

408
00:23:21,547 --> 00:23:22,881
I'll be sure to look for it.

409
00:23:23,424 --> 00:23:25,426
[Jinman] Yes, please do.
I'd appreciate that.

410
00:23:27,052 --> 00:23:28,262
You know what?

411
00:23:29,179 --> 00:23:30,180
[Jinman chuckles]

412
00:23:30,264 --> 00:23:31,181
[Jinman] Whenever I question a suspect,

413
00:23:31,265 --> 00:23:34,810
the most common alibi
is that they were at the theater.

414
00:23:34,893 --> 00:23:36,603
If you had told me you were at home,

415
00:23:36,687 --> 00:23:39,398
I could have confirmed with
the surveillance cameras pretty easily.

416
00:23:39,857 --> 00:23:41,859
Unfortunately, the movie theaters
are trickier.

417
00:23:43,318 --> 00:23:45,404
[Jinman] Did you drive to the theater?

418
00:23:46,321 --> 00:23:48,198
-Well, no.
-[Jinman] Ah.

419
00:23:48,282 --> 00:23:49,992
[Dokyung] It's not a big deal.
It's honestly nothing.

420
00:23:50,075 --> 00:23:52,953
Just wait for my call and then bring
a van to the location I tell you.

421
00:23:53,037 --> 00:23:54,163
That's all.

422
00:23:54,997 --> 00:23:55,998
No.

423
00:23:56,081 --> 00:23:57,458
[exhales]

424
00:23:57,541 --> 00:23:58,917
Get out.

425
00:23:59,001 --> 00:24:00,169
Do it yourself.

426
00:24:00,252 --> 00:24:01,670
Don't even think about involving me.

427
00:24:01,754 --> 00:24:03,422
It's a billion.

428
00:24:03,505 --> 00:24:04,882
Is this what you meant
by giving me what I wanted?

429
00:24:04,965 --> 00:24:06,675
Yujin! Are you listening?

430
00:24:06,759 --> 00:24:08,719
Not a million.
It's a billion won.

431
00:24:08,802 --> 00:24:10,721
Don't you think that amount
is worth betting on?

432
00:24:10,804 --> 00:24:11,930
[Yujin] Betting?

433
00:24:12,014 --> 00:24:14,558
Your whole life is just one big gamble.

434
00:24:15,350 --> 00:24:16,602
No.

435
00:24:16,685 --> 00:24:19,813
[Yujin] It just never ends with you.
There will always be more.

436
00:24:19,897 --> 00:24:21,899
You'll keep doing this until it kills you.

437
00:24:23,108 --> 00:24:25,027
[Yujin] But you don't get to ruin my life,
too, so get out.

438
00:24:25,903 --> 00:24:28,781
[groans]
Yujin, we're so close. You can't-

439
00:24:28,864 --> 00:24:30,616
don't-don't tell me
you're bailing out now!

440
00:24:32,993 --> 00:24:34,745
[Yujin] Dokyung, this isn't fun anymore.

441
00:24:34,828 --> 00:24:37,414
-What?
-[Yujin] Get out.

442
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:40,459
I said go.

443
00:24:43,337 --> 00:24:44,338
[exhales sharply]

444
00:24:45,464 --> 00:24:48,467
[car engine turns over]

445
00:24:52,805 --> 00:24:55,390
-Am I a suspect?
-[Jinman] Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

446
00:24:55,474 --> 00:24:59,269
I'm just saying, it's quite a coincidence,
the whole theater thing. Yeah.

447
00:24:59,353 --> 00:25:00,729
[Jinman] I get it, though.

448
00:25:03,941 --> 00:25:05,109
[Jinman] Hmm.

449
00:25:06,276 --> 00:25:08,654
So what's going to happen
to Lee Dokyung after all this?

450
00:25:08,737 --> 00:25:13,075
[Jinman] Ah, well, he'll be transferred
to a detention center upon recovery

451
00:25:13,158 --> 00:25:15,702
and then depending on
the outcome of his trial,

452
00:25:15,786 --> 00:25:18,622
I'd say he'll likely serve
a year or two in prison.

453
00:25:18,705 --> 00:25:21,083
I thought you told me you hadn't found
the casket yet.

454
00:25:21,166 --> 00:25:24,586
[Yujin] If there's no evidence,
will he still go to jail?

455
00:25:24,670 --> 00:25:26,964
No, but I'm sure we'll find
the casket soon. Yeah.

456
00:25:27,047 --> 00:25:28,048
Oh.

457
00:25:29,675 --> 00:25:30,676
[Jinman] Well, then,

458
00:25:30,759 --> 00:25:33,053
I think that's just about everything
I wanted to ask you.

459
00:25:34,388 --> 00:25:37,307
That means I need to speak
with Kim Heeju next.

460
00:25:37,391 --> 00:25:42,062
So are you able to call her here for me,
or do I go somewhere else?

461
00:25:42,146 --> 00:25:44,064
-Kim Heeju?
-Yeah.

462
00:25:44,148 --> 00:25:48,152
Kim Heeju's alibi
hasn't been confirmed yet?

463
00:25:48,235 --> 00:25:49,987
No, we haven't been able
to get a hold of her,

464
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:51,864
so her alibi is still unclear.

465
00:25:52,823 --> 00:25:54,533
Heeju resigned recently.

466
00:25:55,659 --> 00:25:58,537
She resigned? Why?

467
00:25:58,620 --> 00:26:00,706
She said it was personal.

468
00:26:01,623 --> 00:26:02,624
Oh.

469
00:26:04,251 --> 00:26:05,377
Really?

470
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:06,670
TEAM LEADER
CHA YUJIN

471
00:26:06,753 --> 00:26:10,090
If you can't reach her, I'll give her
a call and tell her to contact you, okay?

472
00:26:10,174 --> 00:26:12,593
Ah, yeah, if you could do that,
I'd appreciate it.

473
00:26:13,677 --> 00:26:15,554
Apologies for barging in earlier.

474
00:26:16,346 --> 00:26:17,347
Yeah.

475
00:26:18,432 --> 00:26:19,892
Did you buy that yourself?

476
00:26:19,975 --> 00:26:21,143
No, it was a gift.

477
00:26:21,727 --> 00:26:22,728
Gotcha.

478
00:26:23,645 --> 00:26:26,690
Again, apologies for earlier.
Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

479
00:26:36,325 --> 00:26:38,035
[machines beeping]

480
00:26:38,118 --> 00:26:39,620
What's going on with belt two?

481
00:26:39,703 --> 00:26:43,081
[Heeju] It's all the metal decorations
attached to the casket.

482
00:26:44,041 --> 00:26:45,042
Let it go through.

483
00:26:46,919 --> 00:26:49,922
[machine rumbling]

484
00:27:06,772 --> 00:27:10,275
[Yujin] He's gonna ask where you were
when Lee Dokyung had his accident.

485
00:27:11,235 --> 00:27:12,236
Come up with an alibi.

486
00:27:17,616 --> 00:27:18,867
[car horn honks]

487
00:27:22,162 --> 00:27:23,914
Heeju!

488
00:27:23,997 --> 00:27:26,124
[♪ ballad playing over stereo]

489
00:27:39,346 --> 00:27:41,098
[Woogy grunts]

490
00:27:45,018 --> 00:27:46,979
You bought a car?

491
00:27:47,062 --> 00:27:49,606
I bought a new car.
Like it?

492
00:27:49,690 --> 00:27:52,317
The sound is insane.
It's fucking surround sound!

493
00:27:52,401 --> 00:27:55,153
[cheers]

494
00:27:56,238 --> 00:27:59,992
Heeju, you should buy a car or something,
too.

495
00:28:00,075 --> 00:28:01,410
[Woogy grunts]

496
00:28:02,911 --> 00:28:05,330
We already paid the goldsmith one potato.

497
00:28:05,414 --> 00:28:08,000
And I took four out of the 12
as my share.

498
00:28:08,083 --> 00:28:09,584
[Woogy] And that's the rest.

499
00:28:09,668 --> 00:28:13,171
[Woogy] 800 million.

500
00:28:14,923 --> 00:28:16,425
We really did it.

501
00:28:17,384 --> 00:28:18,385
I told you.

502
00:28:19,386 --> 00:28:22,597
Heeju, have you ever seen so much cash?

503
00:28:22,681 --> 00:28:24,474
[Woogy] Couldn't even imagine it!

504
00:28:24,558 --> 00:28:25,851
It's crazy!

505
00:28:25,934 --> 00:28:27,519
We're loaded now!

506
