765
00:43:42,558 --> 00:43:43,851
[Heeju] Yes.

766
00:43:43,935 --> 00:43:45,561
But before that...

767
00:43:46,604 --> 00:43:48,981
...you have to drop
the charges against auntie.

768
00:43:50,816 --> 00:43:52,818
Sure, no problem.

769
00:43:52,902 --> 00:43:54,946
Then the three of us can live together.

770
00:43:55,029 --> 00:43:57,323
We're family after all, aren't we?

771
00:43:57,406 --> 00:43:58,491
No.

772
00:44:01,577 --> 00:44:03,287
Auntie isn't doing very well.

773
00:44:04,372 --> 00:44:05,373
It's cancer.

774
00:44:06,165 --> 00:44:07,708
She might not live long.

775
00:44:09,377 --> 00:44:11,087
So I want her to get treated.

776
00:44:11,712 --> 00:44:13,339
In a hospital.

777
00:44:13,422 --> 00:44:16,968
While there's still time
and she can live comfortably.

778
00:44:17,051 --> 00:44:18,970
[Heeju] I'll stay by her side
while she's there.

779
00:44:19,553 --> 00:44:20,763
But uncle...

780
00:44:21,722 --> 00:44:24,016
...you're going to leave town
and not come back.

781
00:44:26,018 --> 00:44:27,812
Why would I?

782
00:44:29,188 --> 00:44:30,648
See, the thing is,

783
00:44:30,731 --> 00:44:33,025
the house and the shop are here,
so where would I go?

784
00:44:33,109 --> 00:44:34,694
[Heeju] You can sell the pawnshop to me.

785
00:44:36,320 --> 00:44:37,905
I've already looked into it.

786
00:44:37,989 --> 00:44:41,784
I know all about the loans and that
the shop is being used as collateral.

787
00:44:41,867 --> 00:44:45,037
I'll take over your debts,
pay you the rest...

788
00:44:45,871 --> 00:44:47,331
...and I'll even pay in cash.

789
00:44:48,749 --> 00:44:49,959
How much?

790
00:44:51,794 --> 00:44:53,838
How much do you want for it?

791
00:44:56,465 --> 00:45:00,136
I won't sell it at market price. Hm.

792
00:45:01,387 --> 00:45:03,764
Maybe for a billion won,
I'd let you have it.

793
00:45:03,848 --> 00:45:05,349
Okay.

794
00:45:08,311 --> 00:45:09,729
Seriously?

795
00:45:09,812 --> 00:45:12,648
You got that kinda cash?
That much?

796
00:45:14,734 --> 00:45:15,735
Yeah.

797
00:45:16,944 --> 00:45:18,029
Is that so?

798
00:45:18,988 --> 00:45:21,073
For that kind of money...

799
00:45:21,991 --> 00:45:24,076
[Heeju] Come to the pawnshop
by 10:00 o'clock tonight.

800
00:45:25,119 --> 00:45:27,163
I'll have the contract
and the money ready for you.

801
00:45:27,246 --> 00:45:28,247
But first...

802
00:45:29,915 --> 00:45:31,542
...you need to drop the charges.

803
00:45:32,335 --> 00:45:33,586
Or the deal's off.

804
00:45:34,503 --> 00:45:35,671
Mm-hmm.

805
00:45:36,630 --> 00:45:37,673
Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

806
00:45:52,188 --> 00:45:53,397
[exhales sharply]

807
00:45:53,939 --> 00:45:55,066
[grunts]

808
00:45:59,570 --> 00:46:00,905
How did it go?

809
00:46:00,988 --> 00:46:03,491
One billion to take his debt
and the store.

810
00:46:03,574 --> 00:46:05,284
Ah, shit, that's crazy.

811
00:46:06,327 --> 00:46:09,955
A billion won for that crumbling,
one-story building? Really?

812
00:46:10,039 --> 00:46:12,291
-Drop me off at Yangpo Airport.
-[Woogy] Why?

813
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:14,919
I'm a bit short on cash.

814
00:46:15,002 --> 00:46:16,212
How much more do you need?

815
00:46:16,962 --> 00:46:19,298
I can have it ready
for you in just two days.

816
00:46:19,382 --> 00:46:23,260
No, it has to be today.
I want to get my aunt out quickly.

817
00:46:23,344 --> 00:46:24,762
[exhales sharply]

818
00:46:24,845 --> 00:46:26,764
We're fucked. Shit.

819
00:46:28,599 --> 00:46:31,018
Let me just lend it to you, okay?

820
00:46:34,688 --> 00:46:36,065
CONFIRMATION OF SEVERANCE PAY RECEIPT
KIM HEEJU

821
00:46:36,148 --> 00:46:39,318
[announcement chiming over speakers]

822
00:46:39,402 --> 00:46:42,154
[Female Announcer] We will now
begin boarding.

823
00:46:46,158 --> 00:46:48,702
I'll tell them to send it out immediately,
since it seems urgent.

824
00:46:48,786 --> 00:46:51,247
Oh, thank you very much.
I appreciate it, Ms. Cha.

825
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:53,416
Where are you living nowadays, Heeju?

826
00:46:53,499 --> 00:46:54,417
What?

827
00:46:55,334 --> 00:46:57,628
I decided to take a look at your resume.

828
00:46:57,711 --> 00:47:00,297
Your address and listed family are fake.

829
00:47:02,049 --> 00:47:03,759
[Yujin] What exactly are you hiding?

830
00:47:05,803 --> 00:47:08,347
-I'm staying with my aunt.
-[Yujin] Oh, really?

831
00:47:08,431 --> 00:47:10,391
And where does your aunt live?

832
00:47:11,434 --> 00:47:12,476
In Jeongsan.

833
00:47:13,310 --> 00:47:14,645
Jeongsan?

834
00:47:15,229 --> 00:47:18,732
[Jinman] Have you been to Jeongsan,
by any chance, recently?

835
00:47:18,816 --> 00:47:20,609
-No.
-[Jinman] Okay.

836
00:47:20,693 --> 00:47:22,319
You haven't then.

837
00:47:22,403 --> 00:47:24,238
-Why are you asking?
-[Jinman inhales sharply]

838
00:47:24,738 --> 00:47:26,490
[Jinman] Seems the smuggling
accomplice went

839
00:47:26,574 --> 00:47:28,701
to Jeongsan with the casket.

840
00:47:30,244 --> 00:47:31,245
[inhales]

841
00:47:33,038 --> 00:47:34,248
There's no way.

842
00:47:35,291 --> 00:47:37,084
You're the accomplice.

843
00:47:38,085 --> 00:47:39,170
What?

844
00:47:40,045 --> 00:47:41,755
Have you given your alibi?

845
00:47:41,839 --> 00:47:44,675
Uh, no, not yet.

846
00:47:44,758 --> 00:47:45,759
Okay, well...

847
00:47:46,969 --> 00:47:49,555
...give the detective a call.
Do that first.

848
00:47:49,638 --> 00:47:51,432
[Yujin] It might be best
to get ahead of it.

849
00:47:51,515 --> 00:47:54,435
Just don't mention you're in Jeongsan,
because the thing is,

850
00:47:54,518 --> 00:47:56,979
the police know that the van carrying
the casket went there.

851
00:47:57,062 --> 00:47:59,690
[Yujin] Heeju, they're gonna find you.

852
00:47:59,773 --> 00:48:01,192
It's only a matter of time.

853
00:48:04,195 --> 00:48:07,448
I'm not sure I know
what you're talking about.

854
00:48:07,531 --> 00:48:08,782
[exhales]

855
00:48:10,201 --> 00:48:11,243
Okay.

856
00:48:12,328 --> 00:48:14,747
Can't blame you, I guess.

857
00:48:14,830 --> 00:48:15,998
Lee Dokyung is a bad guy.

858
00:48:17,249 --> 00:48:18,626
[Yujin] Didn't I ever tell you?

859
00:48:18,709 --> 00:48:19,710
No?

860
00:48:20,836 --> 00:48:23,047
Lee Dokyung and I dated for a while.

861
00:48:24,340 --> 00:48:25,549
[Yujin] Not anymore, though.

862
00:48:27,009 --> 00:48:29,345
I was on National Route 6 that day, too.

863
00:48:30,095 --> 00:48:32,973
He asked me to help him move the casket.

864
00:48:33,057 --> 00:48:35,559
Obviously, I refused to help out.

865
00:48:35,643 --> 00:48:37,561
You were clearly too blinded
by love, though.

866
00:48:38,521 --> 00:48:39,522
[Yujin] It made you foolish.

867
00:48:41,023 --> 00:48:44,443
He has as lover
in every location he flies to
STYLE
::cue()

868
00:48:44,527 --> 00:48:46,237
I bet you didn't know that.

869
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:50,199
China, Hong Kong, Vietnam, Japan.

870
00:48:52,284 --> 00:48:54,286
[Yujin] There are probably more here, too,
that we don't know about.

871
00:48:55,579 --> 00:48:58,165
Do you think he actually loves
all those women?

872
00:48:59,333 --> 00:49:00,417
Or are you telling yourself,

873
00:49:00,501 --> 00:49:05,673
those relationships are all fake,
and you're the only one he truly loves?

874
00:49:08,676 --> 00:49:10,094
[exhales]

875
00:49:10,928 --> 00:49:14,682
I seriously don't know what you mean
by any of these things.

876
00:49:17,101 --> 00:49:19,103
Ms. Cha, why are you telling me all this?

877
00:49:20,020 --> 00:49:21,063
I'm trying to help you.

878
00:49:22,273 --> 00:49:24,608
We're suspects.

879
00:49:24,692 --> 00:49:27,194
As long as you're in the clear,
then I'm in the clear.

880
00:49:28,362 --> 00:49:32,700
[Yujin] Lee Dokyung is just using you
and you keep letting him.

881
00:49:34,034 --> 00:49:35,202
He's not worth it.

882
00:49:36,495 --> 00:49:38,831
I wish you had just run off
with the casket yourself.

883
00:49:38,914 --> 00:49:40,249
That would have been better.

884
00:49:41,333 --> 00:49:44,378
[Yujin] But could you really hold out
on your own with the casket,

885
00:49:44,461 --> 00:49:46,130
until Lee Dokyung gets outta jail?

886
00:49:52,595 --> 00:49:54,054
Remember this, Heeju.

887
00:49:55,014 --> 00:49:56,974
I'm the only person on your side now.

888
00:49:57,057 --> 00:50:00,811
If something happens,
you should call me immediately.

889
00:50:00,894 --> 00:50:02,187
[Yujin] I can help you out.

890
00:50:19,997 --> 00:50:22,499
[inhales and exhales deeply]

891
00:50:38,557 --> 00:50:40,976
What? Are they not gonna pay you?

892
00:50:42,019 --> 00:50:43,687
Want me to take care of it?

893
00:50:43,771 --> 00:50:45,105
No.

894
00:50:46,440 --> 00:50:47,775
[cell phone vibrates]

895
00:50:47,858 --> 00:50:48,859
[phone clicks]

896
00:50:48,942 --> 00:50:50,069
[exhales]

897
00:50:53,155 --> 00:50:54,198
THIS IS DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN.
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU SEE THIS MESSAGE.

898
00:50:54,281 --> 00:50:55,282
I'M CONTACTING YOU FOR A WITNESS
INTERVIEW. I HAVE A FEW THINGS TO ASK YOU.

899
00:50:56,325 --> 00:50:58,243
-Ah, shit.
-[Woogy] What?

900
00:50:58,327 --> 00:51:00,287
Who is it?

901
00:51:00,371 --> 00:51:02,456
It's the police.

902
00:51:03,374 --> 00:51:04,375
What?

903
00:51:05,292 --> 00:51:06,293
What do they want?

904
00:51:07,336 --> 00:51:09,672
Shit, did that fucker
Han Cheoljung report you?

905
00:51:09,755 --> 00:51:12,633
No, the detective looking for the casket.

906
00:51:12,716 --> 00:51:15,761
He suspects I helped Lee Dokyung.

907
00:51:16,762 --> 00:51:20,057
Sounds like the police also know that
the van went to Jeongsan that day.

908
00:51:25,688 --> 00:51:27,731
Ah, shit.

909
00:51:27,815 --> 00:51:29,650
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
Hold on.

910
00:51:29,733 --> 00:51:30,734
[Woogy] What are you doing?

911
00:51:31,694 --> 00:51:33,987
If I don't call him,
he'll suspect me more.

912
00:51:34,905 --> 00:51:37,074
[exhales]

913
00:51:37,157 --> 00:51:38,242
Hold on a sec.
STYLE
::cue()

914
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:48,419
Put it on speaker, okay?

915
00:51:48,502 --> 00:51:51,171
[cell phone trilling]

916
00:51:52,589 --> 00:51:54,800
[Jinman] This is Detective Kim Jinman

917
00:51:54,883 --> 00:51:56,093
-of the Jeongsan Police.
-Uh...

918
00:51:56,635 --> 00:51:57,636
...yes, hello.

919
00:51:57,720 --> 00:52:00,639
You called because I used
to work at Yango Airport?

920
00:52:00,723 --> 00:52:02,182
-This is Kim Heeju.
-Kim Jinman of Jeongsan?

921
00:52:02,266 --> 00:52:04,393
[Jinman] Oh, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

922
00:52:04,476 --> 00:52:07,980
Seems like Cha Yujin finally managed
to get a hold of you, then.

923
00:52:08,063 --> 00:52:10,816
Anyway, well, I tried calling a bunch.

924
00:52:10,899 --> 00:52:13,610
Then I stopped by your house
but you weren't there either.

925
00:52:13,694 --> 00:52:17,990
I even went to Yangpo Airport
and they told me you left the company.

926
00:52:19,408 --> 00:52:20,951
Is that right?
You no longer work there?

927
00:52:21,034 --> 00:52:26,999
Uh, yeah, I've just been busy
with personal stuff so...

928
00:52:28,083 --> 00:52:29,835
[Jinman] No worries.
Nothing major.

929
00:52:30,836 --> 00:52:32,671
Just need to know where you were the day
of Lee Dokyung's accident.

930
00:52:34,465 --> 00:52:36,842
The date was September fourth,
if you recall.

931
00:52:38,552 --> 00:52:41,638
[Heeju] Uh, after I got off work...

932
00:52:42,765 --> 00:52:47,603
...I remember I drove up to-
to Gangneung for the evening.

933
00:52:47,686 --> 00:52:50,147
[Jinman] Gangneung?
And why go there?

934
00:52:50,230 --> 00:52:51,982
You came all the way back
to work the next day.

935
00:52:53,025 --> 00:52:57,529
[Heeju] Yeah, I just wanted
to clear my head,

936
00:52:57,613 --> 00:52:59,823
so I went shopping
and then went to see a movie.

937
00:52:59,907 --> 00:53:01,283
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

938
00:53:03,118 --> 00:53:06,079
A movie, huh? On your own?

939
00:53:08,165 --> 00:53:09,374
Yeah.

940
00:53:09,458 --> 00:53:10,918
[Jinman] I see.

941
00:53:11,001 --> 00:53:12,377
You don't have a car, right?

942
00:53:13,170 --> 00:53:14,296
No.

943
00:53:14,379 --> 00:53:15,672
[Jinman] Okay, I got it.

944
00:53:15,756 --> 00:53:17,007
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

945
00:53:17,090 --> 00:53:18,258
I'll be able to check
the rest on my end here.

946
00:53:18,342 --> 00:53:20,385
All right, well,
thanks for calling.

947
00:53:21,428 --> 00:53:22,513
Ooh.

948
00:53:22,596 --> 00:53:24,097
Ah, shit!

949
00:53:24,181 --> 00:53:26,141
Kim Jinman's with the company.

950
00:53:26,225 --> 00:53:29,353
-He's a detective.
-Yeah, well, obviously.

951
00:53:29,436 --> 00:53:31,188
But he's a detective who works with us.

952
00:53:33,732 --> 00:53:35,609
Hey, Detective.
Doing okay?

953
00:53:37,569 --> 00:53:39,780
[Woogy] Jeongsan Police,
Investigations Division, right?

954
00:53:40,697 --> 00:53:43,408
That means it's not the fucking cops.
It's Yes Money chasing you.

955
00:53:43,492 --> 00:53:44,993
They want to find their casket.

956
00:53:46,370 --> 00:53:48,956
[Woogy] Ah, we're really fucked now.

957
00:53:49,706 --> 00:53:51,333
[exhales sharply]

958
00:53:53,210 --> 00:53:54,378
-Oh.
-Sir.

959
00:53:54,461 --> 00:53:56,129
Uh, looks like the charges
are being dropped.

960
00:53:56,630 --> 00:53:58,423
-O-open it. I need to talk to her.
-Yes, sir.

961
00:53:58,507 --> 00:53:59,341
Thanks.

962
00:53:59,424 --> 00:54:02,135
[keys rattling]

963
00:54:02,219 --> 00:54:03,887
[Jinman] Ms. Yeo Sunok.

964
00:54:03,971 --> 00:54:05,264
[door creaking]

965
00:54:05,347 --> 00:54:06,640
Yeo Sunok.

966
00:54:07,516 --> 00:54:09,768
What? Miss Yeo Sunok.

967
00:54:11,144 --> 00:54:13,856
Hey, Yeo Sunok.

968
00:54:15,941 --> 00:54:18,277
Sunok. Sunok! Wake up!

969
00:54:18,360 --> 00:54:19,903
Hey, help me out here!

970
00:54:19,987 --> 00:54:21,154
[Male Officer] Yes, sir.

971
00:54:21,238 --> 00:54:22,614
[grunts]

972
00:54:22,698 --> 00:54:24,032
[Jinman] Okay, call 911.

973
00:54:24,116 --> 00:54:26,118
-Call them right now!
-[Male Officer] Yes, sir.

974
00:54:26,201 --> 00:54:29,079
[distant sirens blaring]

975
00:54:37,921 --> 00:54:41,049
[gasping]

976
00:54:41,133 --> 00:54:43,844
[Mija whimpers]

977
00:54:43,927 --> 00:54:45,804
[Mija] Sunok. Sunok, wake up.
Come on.

978
00:54:46,805 --> 00:54:47,806
[Mija gasps]

979
00:54:47,889 --> 00:54:49,600
What's wrong with her?

980
00:54:50,225 --> 00:54:51,935
[Mija] Doc-doctor!

981
00:54:52,019 --> 00:54:53,854
[gasps]
No!

982
00:54:53,937 --> 00:54:55,230
Sunok, no!

983
00:54:55,856 --> 00:54:58,317
Sunok, please, open your eyes!

984
00:54:58,400 --> 00:54:59,651
[Mija crying]
[Mija] Sunok!

985
00:54:59,735 --> 00:55:01,194
Please!

986
00:55:01,278 --> 00:55:03,071
[crying]

987
00:55:04,489 --> 00:55:07,159
[Mija] They said she got blood
in her lungs and went into shock.

988
00:55:07,242 --> 00:55:08,577
Oh, so stupid.

989
00:55:08,660 --> 00:55:11,330
She could have asked them
to take her to the hospital.

990
00:55:11,413 --> 00:55:14,750
But instead she just sat there suffering
with a hole in her lung.

991
00:55:14,833 --> 00:55:16,251
Like she wanted to die.

992
00:55:17,169 --> 00:55:19,004
So, what did you say to your uncle?

993
00:55:19,838 --> 00:55:22,466
He dropped the charges.
How did you manage that?

994
00:55:22,549 --> 00:55:24,051
[inhales deeply]

995
00:55:24,134 --> 00:55:26,970
Will you please do me a favor
and stay with her tonight?

996
00:55:27,054 --> 00:55:27,929
I'll be there tomorrow.

997
00:55:28,013 --> 00:55:29,765
[inhales]

998
00:55:29,848 --> 00:55:31,308
[groans]

999
00:55:31,391 --> 00:55:33,894
Tonight? It's Friday, though.

1000
00:55:34,478 --> 00:55:37,648
[grunts]
I'm supposed to be working tonight.

1001
00:55:38,899 --> 00:55:40,025
[exhales]

1002
00:55:40,108 --> 00:55:43,028
I-I'll pay you a million won
for your trouble.

1003
00:55:44,529 --> 00:55:45,947
[Mija] Okay, okay.

1004
00:55:46,031 --> 00:55:47,866
I'm sorry, auntie.
Thank you.

1005
00:55:48,909 --> 00:55:52,996
[phone beeps]
[inhales and exhales sharply]

1006
00:55:55,791 --> 00:55:56,792
Heeju.

1007
00:56:01,838 --> 00:56:03,173
Let's take a sec to think about it.

1008
00:56:03,256 --> 00:56:04,424
About what?

1009
00:56:06,301 --> 00:56:09,137
[Woogy] About shutting Han Cheoljung up
with hush money.

1010
00:56:09,221 --> 00:56:10,263
How can you be sure?

1011
00:56:11,098 --> 00:56:12,891
That asshole could still
rat you out after.

1012
00:56:14,935 --> 00:56:16,353
The second he gives your name
to the police,

1013
00:56:16,436 --> 00:56:17,979
Detective Kim will find out, too.

1014
00:56:18,855 --> 00:56:21,233
That means he'll know without
a doubt you went to Jeongsan.

1015
00:56:24,111 --> 00:56:25,112
[exhales sharply]

1016
00:56:25,195 --> 00:56:27,531
But he did get my aunt out
like he promised.

1017
00:56:27,614 --> 00:56:28,740
Exactly.

1018
00:56:29,658 --> 00:56:31,576
So you don't have
to worry about her anymore.
STYLE
::cue()

1019
00:56:40,627 --> 00:56:42,170
Didn't you say you wanted him dead?

1020
00:56:43,964 --> 00:56:44,965
[Woogy] Heeju.

1021
00:56:45,048 --> 00:56:46,800
You think it'll end here?

1022
00:56:47,259 --> 00:56:48,301
Not a chance.

1023
00:56:48,385 --> 00:56:50,679
[Woogy] I know assholes
like him too damn well.

1024
00:56:50,762 --> 00:56:53,640
He'll keep coming back,
asking for money again and again.

1025
00:56:57,477 --> 00:56:59,813
[Woogy] As long as you and your aunt
are still here,

1026
00:56:59,896 --> 00:57:00,981
he'll never leave you alone.

1027
00:57:02,315 --> 00:57:05,193
Why put yourself in such
a dangerous situation?

1028
00:57:05,277 --> 00:57:07,070
And if Detective Kim catches you...

1029
00:57:08,155 --> 00:57:09,865
...then it'll all be over, Heeju.

1030
00:57:09,948 --> 00:57:11,825
The gold bars.
Everything.

1031
00:57:13,410 --> 00:57:20,417
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

1032
00:57:34,765 --> 00:57:37,100
Haengbok Pawnshop, huh?

1033
00:57:41,062 --> 00:57:43,148
[door creaks]

1034
00:57:43,231 --> 00:57:44,733
[Cheoljung] Heeju!

1035
00:57:59,080 --> 00:58:00,165
Read it over.

1036
00:58:13,762 --> 00:58:16,097
So, the money.
Where is it?

1037
00:58:16,181 --> 00:58:18,433
I wanna see it myself first.

1038
00:58:18,517 --> 00:58:20,018
[exhales]

1039
00:58:22,103 --> 00:58:23,939
[grunting]

1040
00:58:25,440 --> 00:58:27,108
[Heeju grunts]

1041
00:58:30,028 --> 00:58:31,655
[zipper unzips]

1042
00:58:39,287 --> 00:58:40,205
[Cheoljung gasping]

1043
00:58:40,288 --> 00:58:43,166
I didn't believe you!
What the...

1044
00:58:43,708 --> 00:58:46,503
...what the hell have you been doing
all these years, Heeju?

1045
00:58:46,586 --> 00:58:50,298
[Cheoljung] I mean, how could you
possibly have this kind of money?

1046
00:58:54,636 --> 00:58:55,804
Sign the contract.

1047
00:58:55,887 --> 00:58:58,223
Uh, okay.
Yeah, sure.

1048
00:59:03,228 --> 00:59:04,521
[zipper zipping]

1049
00:59:05,564 --> 00:59:06,898
[exhales]

1050
00:59:07,566 --> 00:59:09,901
You know I can't do it, Heeju.

1051
00:59:13,446 --> 00:59:16,616
[Cheoljung] Let's stop
and think this over again, okay?

1052
00:59:16,700 --> 00:59:19,244
[Cheoljung] Who cares
who owns the pawnshop?

1053
00:59:19,327 --> 00:59:20,495
That doesn't matter.

1054
00:59:21,413 --> 00:59:23,164
Family is all that matters.

1055
00:59:23,248 --> 00:59:26,918
You and me, your aunt,
we should all live together.

1056
00:59:29,254 --> 00:59:30,630
Sign the contract.

1057
00:59:30,714 --> 00:59:32,674
I'm not telling you again.

1058
00:59:33,091 --> 00:59:35,051
[Cheoljun] The whole drive here,

1059
00:59:35,135 --> 00:59:37,053
I put a lotta thought into this.

1060
00:59:37,971 --> 00:59:39,222
[inhales and exhales sharply]

1061
00:59:39,306 --> 00:59:40,432
Your poor aunt.

1062
00:59:40,515 --> 00:59:43,560
[Cheoljung] She has cancer
and not much time to live.

1063
00:59:43,643 --> 00:59:46,855
I just think while she's alive,
she'd be happier if we were all together.

1064
00:59:46,938 --> 00:59:48,398
We're supposed to be family.

1065
00:59:48,481 --> 00:59:49,733
[scoffs]

1066
00:59:49,816 --> 00:59:52,110
[chuckles]

1067
00:59:53,069 --> 00:59:55,113
-Family?
-[Cheoljung] If we weren't family,

1068
00:59:55,196 --> 00:59:58,116
I would've reported you
to the police right away, ya know?

1069
00:59:58,199 --> 01:00:00,785
[Cheoljung] You swung that club at me.

1070
01:00:00,869 --> 01:00:03,371
I saw your face as clear as day.

1071
01:00:04,748 --> 01:00:08,710
[Cheoljung] Or would you rather I go
to the police right now

1072
01:00:08,793 --> 01:00:11,087
and let 'em know it was you?

1073
01:00:14,215 --> 01:00:15,216
[Heeju grunts]

1074
01:00:16,092 --> 01:00:19,095
What should I spend all this money on?
Pay off the loan?

1075
01:00:19,179 --> 01:00:22,223
Well, seeing as it is our store,
let's do that.

1076
01:00:22,307 --> 01:00:25,727
Oh, sweetie, being on your own
was so hard wasn't it?

1077
01:00:32,150 --> 01:00:35,236
No. No! No! No!

1078
01:00:35,320 --> 01:00:37,155
-[grunting]
-Ah, shit.

1079
01:00:37,238 --> 01:00:39,616
[grunting]

1080
01:00:39,699 --> 01:00:41,034
[Cheoljung grunts]

1081
01:00:41,117 --> 01:00:42,661
[slaps]
[Heeju wails]

1082
01:00:42,744 --> 01:00:44,496
Ah, you little shit.

1083
01:00:44,579 --> 01:00:46,706
[Heeju groaning]

1084
01:00:48,208 --> 01:00:50,877
[groaning]

1085
01:00:50,961 --> 01:00:52,963
[Cheoljung] Don't even think
about leaving.

1086
01:00:53,046 --> 01:00:56,174
Just stay here
and look after the pawnshop.

1087
01:00:56,257 --> 01:01:00,220
[Cheoljung] While your aunt dies.

1088
01:01:00,303 --> 01:01:01,763
[snickers]

1089
01:01:01,846 --> 01:01:06,434
[coughing]

1090
01:01:06,518 --> 01:01:09,521
[Heeju gasping]

1091
01:01:14,651 --> 01:01:15,652
Goodbye.

1092
01:01:17,904 --> 01:01:19,656
[groaning and gasping]

1093
01:01:20,699 --> 01:01:22,075
[Heeju] Woogy!

1094
01:01:23,076 --> 01:01:24,995
[door creaking]

1095
01:01:27,539 --> 01:01:28,665
[door lock clicks]

1096
01:01:28,748 --> 01:01:31,167
Bastard, who are you?

1097
01:01:31,251 --> 01:01:34,212
[groaning]

1098
01:01:34,295 --> 01:01:36,840
Evil son of a bitch.
STYLE
::cue()

1099
01:01:42,679 --> 01:01:44,222
Should I do it?

1100
01:01:44,305 --> 01:01:47,308
[clock ticking echoes]

1101
01:01:51,104 --> 01:01:52,105
Yeah.

1102
01:01:54,899 --> 01:01:55,984
Do it.

1103
01:01:56,484 --> 01:01:57,652
[both grunting]
[blade slices]

1104
01:01:57,736 --> 01:02:00,655
[both shouting]

1105
01:02:00,739 --> 01:02:03,742
[pained gasping]

1106
01:02:07,620 --> 01:02:10,248
[both grunting]
[blade slicing]

1107
01:02:19,257 --> 01:02:22,177
[blade piercing]

1108
01:02:22,260 --> 01:02:25,263
[gagging and sputtering]

1109
01:02:29,517 --> 01:02:31,144
[blood squelching]

1110
01:02:31,227 --> 01:02:33,938
[Woogy breathing heavily]

1111
01:02:36,775 --> 01:02:39,778
[♪ dramatic music]

1112
01:02:48,078 --> 01:02:49,412
[blade clatters]

1113
01:02:50,121 --> 01:02:53,166
[both breathing heavily]

1114
01:03:16,064 --> 01:03:19,067
[♪ music continues]

